# Wall relaxation reactions 
# Release energy and excited state was quenching 
# J.M. Hong, S. Pancheshnyi, E. Tam, J.J. Lowke, S. Prawerm, A.B Murphy, Kinetic modelling of NH3 production in N2-H2 non-equilibrium  
# atmospheric-pressure plasma catalysis, J. Phys. D: Appl. Phys. 50(2017) 154005.
# Discharge volume and effective area was confirmed according to experimental reactor, N. Liu, Q. Chen, X.W. Jiang, J. Chen, L.D. Zhang, Combust. Flame, 259 (2024) 113142
# The wall loss possibility was from the textbook, Plasma kinetic in atmospheric-pressure. 
# O.V. Braginskiy, A.N. Vasilieva, K.S. Klopovskiy, A.S. Kovalev, D.V. Lopaev, O.V. Proshina, T.V. Rakhimova, A.T. Rakhimova,
# Singlet oxygen generation in O2 flow excited by RF discharge, I. Homogeneous discharge mode, α-model
# Rate constant is calculated at 60 Torr(8000 Pa).
O2(A1)=>O2                         ! (4.37d-07*8000/(Tgas/300.0d0)**1.5+1.253d-2*2*(2-4.0d-05)/4.0d-05/(21165.67d0*Tgas/32)**0.5)**-1.0
O2(B1)=>O2                         ! (4.37d-07*8000/(Tgas/300.0d0)**1.5+1.253d-2*2*(2-2.0d-02)/2.0d-02/(21165.67d0*Tgas/32)**0.5)**-1.0
O2*=>O2                            ! (4.37d-07*8000/(Tgas/300.0d0)**1.5+1.253d-2*2*(2-1.0d+00)/1.0d+00/(21165.67d0*Tgas/32)**0.5)**-1.0
# estimated                                                                                           
N2(A)=>N2                          ! (4.37d-07*8000/(Tgas/300.0d0)**1.5+1.253d-2*2*(2-1.0d+00)/1.0d+00/(21165.67d0*Tgas/28)**0.5)**-1.0
N2(B)=>N2                          ! (4.37d-07*8000/(Tgas/300.0d0)**1.5+1.253d-2*2*(2-1.0d+00)/1.0d+00/(21165.67d0*Tgas/28)**0.5)**-1.0
N2(A')=>N2                         ! (4.37d-07*8000/(Tgas/300.0d0)**1.5+1.253d-2*2*(2-1.0d+00)/1.0d+00/(21165.67d0*Tgas/28)**0.5)**-1.0
N2(C)=>N2                          ! (4.37d-07*8000/(Tgas/300.0d0)**1.5+1.253d-2*2*(2-1.0d+00)/1.0d+00/(21165.67d0*Tgas/28)**0.5)**-1.0
## γ was estimated by O(1D)                                                                             
CH3OH(e1)=>CH3OH                   ! (4.37d-07*8000/(Tgas/300.0d0)**1.5+1.253d-2*2*(2-1.0d+00)/1.0d+00/(21165.67d0*Tgas/32)**0.5)**-1.0
CH3OH(e2)=>CH3OH                   ! (4.37d-07*8000/(Tgas/300.0d0)**1.5+1.253d-2*2*(2-1.0d+00)/1.0d+00/(21165.67d0*Tgas/32)**0.5)**-1.0
CH3OH(e3)=>CH3OH                   ! (4.37d-07*8000/(Tgas/300.0d0)**1.5+1.253d-2*2*(2-1.0d+00)/1.0d+00/(21165.67d0*Tgas/32)**0.5)**-1.0

O(1D)=>O                           ! (4.37d-07*8000/(Tgas/300.0d0)**1.5+1.253d-2*2*(2-1.0d+00)/1.0d+00/(21165.67d0*Tgas/16)**0.5)**-1.0
